PRINTED PARAGRAPHS WITHIN EACH STREAM
For every join, inspect the preceding retained ending and this opening WITHIN THAT DESTINATION. A block's unfinished ending completed on the next page does not establish an incoming join to an earlier block. A complete question followed by an explanation may be two paragraphs. A quotation may contain multiple paragraphs; quotation scope and argumentative cohesion do not justify merging them. A short completed line ending before the normal right edge, followed by first-line-only indentation, is evidence of a new printed paragraph.

printed_lines reports raster observations, not semantic verdicts. median_ink_height is measured ink height; Compare an unnumbered tail with both main prose and preceding notes using these observations and literal seams, never fixed size thresholds. A first_line_extra_indent_vs_later_lines_in_same_box is RELATIVE TO LATER LINES IN THE SAME BOX: whole-quotation or column indentation is already subtracted. A positive value can establish a new paragraph INSIDE a note, not body ownership. Missing observations are unknown. printed_lines.left_offsets are local observed line starts; a multi-line bbox's left edge is not necessarily its first-line start. Source geometry does not change when slicing, and observations for the original first line cannot be invented for later slices.

